  "id": "ependymal-cell",
  "term": "ependymal cell",
  "definition": "An ependymal cell is a cell that develops from radial glial cells lining the brain’s ventricles during early postnatal development. These cells form a flattened lining with multiple motile cilia and are important for the barrier between brain tissue and cerebrospinal fluid and for moving cerebrospinal fluid.",
